  "e.src_note": "★<strong>The megawatts on the slider are megawatts</strong>: the Gaussian deposition is normalised by its <strong>volume integral</strong>, so ∫Q dV is the power you asked for — which is what makes W<sub>th</sub>, τ<sub>E</sub> and Q reportable at all (the 1.5-D bar's source is a temperature rate in arbitrary units, and it <strong>cannot</strong> report them, nor does it pretend to). ★Every physical term is a kernel entry: the alphas are Bosch-Hale reactivity with the Stix partition, the exchange the classical collision rate, the resistivity Spitzer's <em>formula</em> tier (the neoclassical trapped-particle correction is <strong>not</strong> folded in), the bootstrap the Redl-2021 analytic model. ★<strong>Radiation is the ADAS cooling rate summed over the whole composition</strong>: the bulk ion enters as a hydrogen isotope (the table's H/D/T coefficients are identical) and the impurity is picked from <strong>the kernel's own ADAS table</strong> (the menu is asked for at load, never written into the page), at a prescribed n<sub>z</sub> = c·n<sub>e</sub>. ★★This was once wrong: a species left unnamed contributes <strong>nothing</strong> to the ADAS sum, so “no impurity” came back as a deuterium plasma that <strong>did not radiate at all</strong>. What is reported now is the ADAS total. ★The “non-bremsstrahlung” figure beside it is that total <strong>minus the same entry's NRL bremsstrahlung estimate</strong> — a <strong>decomposition</strong> of one answer rather than a second model: for pure deuterium the two agree to a few per cent at keV temperatures, and what the ADAS curve carries below 300 eV that the formula does not is exactly this difference. ★The impurity does <strong>not</strong> enter quasi-neutrality: this tier still runs the resistivity and the bootstrap on the Z<sub>eff</sub> control with an undiluted bulk ion. The implied Z<sub>eff</sub> = 1 + c·Z(Z−1) and dilution n<sub>i</sub>/n<sub>e</sub> = 1 − Z·c are <strong>reported in the readings</strong> for you to judge against it. ★The driven current and the fuelling are <strong>prescribed Gaussians</strong>, not deposition models: no NBI ray tracing, no pellets, no gas puff. ★The Ohmic power is σ<sub>∥</sub>E<sub>∥</sub>², with E<sub>∥</sub> = −2πρ(∂ψ/∂t)/V′ from the flux the march is itself moving — the <strong>current channel's own</strong> relation between a moving flux and the current it drives (equate its source term with σE), not a separate model. It is <strong>lagged by one step</strong> (the rate is measured across the step just taken), so the first step's Ohmic power is zero.",

