  "e.freeiter": "Free-boundary iteration cap",
  "e.freeiter_note": "★<strong>A budget, not a criterion.</strong> The tolerance is fixed at 1e-9 (the fixed-boundary refinement is held to the same number); what this sets is only how long the solver may look. ★★<strong>Since v108 the solver terminates on its own with a three-way verdict</strong>: converged (residual within tolerance AND the mask unchanged over consecutive rounds), <strong>settled</strong> (the answer has stopped moving while mask-quantisation jitter floors the residual above the tolerance — more rounds change nothing; see T-M16), or budget exhausted. The droop trim still resets its reference on every tolerance hit, but the settled exit stops it circling. ★<strong>Measured (EAST\u2019s reference discharge, the solve this page does by default, after the boundary-rule fix)</strong>: cap 20 → budget exhausted, residual 6.7e-2; 100 → exhausted, 1.2e-3; <strong>600 (the default) → settled on its own at iteration 111</strong>, residual floor 6.2e-4, diverted configuration; 10000 → bit-identical to 600. <strong>The default 600 is therefore a sufficient budget</strong> — this equilibrium reaches its own verdict inside it; the old \u201cfirst converges at 7787 iterations\u201d reading belonged to the pre-fix limiter solution and no longer holds. For cases that can truly converge (no mask jitter), this still sets how long the solver looks.",
