  "e.beam.needs_psi": "★NBI deposition needs a <strong>ψ<sub>N</sub> map on the (R, Z) grid</strong>: the solved equilibrium and an imported g-file have one, the analytic (Miller) tier does not. So it is <strong>disabled</strong> here rather than attenuating a chord through a made-up flux map — that would report a stopping depth nobody computed.",
  "e.beam_note": "★★The whole chain is the kernel's: the rays over the beam's finite cross-section, their geometry, <code>pitch(R) = R<sub>tan</sub>/R</code>, reading the profile at the ray's <strong>own</strong> samples, the Janev stopping cross-section, the attenuation and the shell binning are <strong>one</strong> <code>beam_deposit</code> call; the Stix critical energy and slowing time are <code>beam_slowing</code>; the electron/ion split and τ<sub>eff</sub> are <code>beam_energy_partition</code>; the electron shielding is <code>beam_shielding</code>; the driven current is <code>beam_current</code>; the first-orbit-loss mask is <code>first_orbit_loss</code>. This side only does the <strong>assembly</strong>, and it is the same assembly <code>fylite.scenario.model.nbi.deposit</code> performs. ★<strong>What is not here</strong>: ICRH / ECRH (the physics is in Rust, there is no C entry), pellets, gas puffing (★<strong>LH is wired now</strong>, but as <strong>its own switch</strong> — a different launcher, a different band and different damping physics, and the two are never collapsed into one \"auxiliary heating\"); the fast-ion pressure is an <strong>isotropic</strong> scalar (a tangential beam is not), and the torque is still the slider's total borrowing only the beam's <strong>shape</strong>. ★The beam is re-evaluated on the <strong>coupling cadence</strong> (once with frozen geometry): the attenuation follows n<sub>e</sub>/T<sub>e</sub>, and putting a ray trace inside the per-step loop buys less accuracy than that cadence already bounds.",
